#>chapter_26_ecology
#:ecology #!book-2
#:layer #!pragmatics
#:status #!live

~<rationale>{
  Chapter 26 measured from its canon. Ring 13 of 13, ^ integration: summary, emission, and octave recursion. Its rooms can be read as the stations of one line, in order; its twin an octave away is Chapter 13.
}

^"identity"{
  chapter: 26
  book: 2
  ring: 13
  title: "The Feast of the Uneven Slice"
  mood: "reflection"
  period: "turning"
  logline: "At the Turning of the Year, Bonk City's Great Table spans plaza, gate, and river mist — and asks for exactly one spill so an unclosed circle can turn onward without resetting."
  epigraph: "Exactly one pie spills, the sliver stays unrounded, and the ring turns cleanly on."
}

^"grammar"{
  construct: "^"
  construct_name: "integration"
  construct_kind: "integration"
  opening_lens: "capstone bind gathering the twelve preceding steps"
  closing_perspective: "hinges into the next ring (~)"
